    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Coding</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Linked list</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Linked Lists: Dummy Heads, Fast/Slow Pointers and In-Place Rewiring</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Almost every linked-list interview question is one of six moves: a dummy head, a fast/slow pointer pair, a three-pointer reversal, a splice-merge, a block reversal, or a copy that weaves new nodes between old ones. This page teaches each move with a picture, gives one tested template per move in Go, C++, Java and Python, and shows how to spot which move a question wants.</p>\r\n",
